Description:

Powerful tool that can be used to explore the Mandelbulb in a generic form
involving three power variations, plus the classic power 8. Those powers
are calculated in sequence then summed up.
You can combine the formulas for z^8, z^6, z^3 and z like this;

z = z^8 + rotate*(sc3*z^3 + sc4*z^4 + sc6*z^6) + C;

Power 3 introduces asymmetry in Julia shapes. It might be interesting to put
it in a mix, however.
I haven't put power 2 in because it tends to disturb a lot the shapes.
Originally the formula had more rotations, have been taken off because
it was too slow.

Notes on ZMul:
Should be set to -1, 1 or zero.
When it is set to zero, power 8 is discarded and the formula changes to;

z = rotate*(sc3*z^3 + sc4*z^4 + sc6*z^6) + C;

That mode is interesting to explore many lower power only variations.

If not zero, it multiplies z component to get the negative z variant.
Just for power 8, because you may get the same result for lower
powers using rotations.
Cool results can be achieved combining negative z power 8 with positive
z low powers. 